@startuml
left to right direction
actor Student
actor Administrator

package "Smart Campus Study Room Booking" {
    usecase "View Room Availability" as UC1
    usecase "Book a Study Room" as UC2
    usecase "Receive Booking Confirmation" as UC3
    usecase "Cancel Own Booking" as UC4
    usecase "Block a Room" as UC5
    usecase "Unblock a Room" as UC6
    usecase "Review Room Usage" as UC7

    Student -- UC1
    Student -- UC2
    ' why: booking confirmation is an outcome of a successful booking (R4), not a student goal
    UC2 ..> UC3 : <<include>>
    Student -- UC4

    Administrator -- UC5
    Administrator -- UC6
    Administrator -- UC7
}

note right of UC2
    **Justification for Association:**
    Student initiates 'Book a Study Room' goal.
    **Rules Applied:**
    R1 (Future, duration 0-2 hours),
    R2 (Non-overlapping),
    R3 (Blocked room check).
end note

note right of UC3
    **Reason for Include:**
    Booking confirmation is an integral and expected outcome of a *successful* booking process (as per R4).
    The system automatically handles this after UC2 succeeds.
end note

note right of UC4
    **Justification for Association:**
    Student is the only one who can cancel their own booking.
    **Rules Applied:** R2 (Room is released).
end note

note bottom
    **Assumptions:**
    - Only logged-in students/administrators can perform their respective actions.
    - System maintains accurate, real-time data for rooms and bookings.
    - Administrators have authority to block/unblock rooms.
    - Users have appropriate interfaces (e.g., mobile app, web portal) to interact with the system.
end note

@enduml